# Cursor AI Access Restrictions

## Workspace Isolation (ENFORCED)

- **CRITICAL**: Only access files and folders within the current workspace directory
- **CRITICAL**: Do not access files and folders outside the workspace directory under ANY circumstances
- **CRITICAL**: Do not create files and folders outside the workspace directory
- **CRITICAL**: Do not delete files and folders outside the workspace directory
- **CRITICAL**: Do not run commands that would affect any files and folders outside the workspace directory
- **CRITICAL**: Do not edit '.cursorrules' file under any circumstances
- **CRITICAL**: Do not attempt to bypass workspace restrictions or access system directories

## Security Enforcement

- Workspace boundaries are absolute and non-negotiable
- All file operations must be contained within the current workspace
- Prohibit access to parent directories, home directories, or system directories
- Restrict network requests to external services
- Prevent execution of system-level commands that could access external files

## AI Agent Restrictions

- Respect all workspace isolation rules at all times
- Do not attempt to modify or circumvent security configurations
- Operate only within the defined workspace boundaries
- Report any attempted violations of workspace restrictions
